+## INLINEGROUP01: direct scan of inline grouped postings (2026-09-26)
+
+Official PostgreSQL 18 index locking contract re-read:
+https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/index-locking.html. This change stays in
+pin-core's grouped scan. It changes no PG binding, buffer lock, WAL write,
+on-disk format, snapshot, or visibility operation. The existing bitmap scan
+continues to return heap candidates under PostgreSQL's MVCC rules.
+
+Catalog inline postings are already parsed and checked by Value::read. The
+reader checks the actual heap layout's maximum offset again before constructing
+fixed-size page masks. The scan uses these masks directly, avoiding temporary
+bitmap encoding and decoding. Record-backed postings retain the original path.
+No inline coordinate is emitted without the same group mask and offset checks.
+The existing grouped storage and query oracle tests cover inline and record
+entries; native SQL identity and paired backend CPU are required to retain it.
+
 Review: the same live relation and full-CAPACITY exclusive extent prove the
 relocated FFI call. New oracle tests compare fresh/reloaded images across kinds,
 assert stable buffer address, exercise failures/recovery and preserve zero tails.
